# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# How to load these
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the REQUIRED block below — that's all most
# setups need. A plain `.env` works everywhere; in DEV we personally inject with
# Infisical instead of a committed file:
#   infisical run --path=/<your-project> -- pnpm dev
#
# Only two things are ever truly required: APP_SECRET + model access. Everything
# under "Optional" has a working default. WHERE you put these differs per host (a
# .env file locally, the Vercel / Mastra Cloud dashboard in the cloud, Coolify on a
# VPS) — but the variable NAMES are identical everywhere.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — local AND production
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Min 32 chars. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
APP_SECRET=

# ── Model access — choose ONE style ──
#
# (A) GATEWAY  ← easiest if you switch models a lot: ONE key unlocks every provider.
#     Switch models by changing CHAT_MODEL alone — you NEVER add another key. The kit
#     routes BOTH of these natively, so pick whichever you already have (or neither →
#     use direct keys). Set the key + a matching CHAT_MODEL prefix:
#       • Vercel AI Gateway:  AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY     + CHAT_MODEL=vercel/anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6
#       • Mastra Gateway:     MASTRA_GATEWAY_API_KEY + CHAT_MODEL=mastra/anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6
#     (Vercel AI Gateway = free monthly credits, https://vercel.com/ai-gateway · Mastra
#      Gateway = free account, https://gateway.mastra.ai. You can swap between them anytime
#      — it's just the key + the CHAT_MODEL prefix.)
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
# MASTRA_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
#
# (B) DIRECT   ← simplest if you only ever use ONE provider.
#     A provider key unlocks ONLY that provider — OPENAI_API_KEY gives you OpenAI models
#     only, so mixing GPT + Claude means adding BOTH keys. This is the out-of-the-box
#     default (CHAT_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6), so ANTHROPIC_API_KEY alone works:
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION ONLY — self-hosted (VPS / Docker / Coolify)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev needs NOTHING here — storage defaults to a file (./mastra.db). A deployed
# server has no persistent local disk, so point at a Turso database instead:
#   TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://<db>-<org>.turso.io
#   TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=<from `turso db tokens create <db>`>
# Prefer Postgres? See docs/postgres.md.
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL=
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mastra Cloud (managed hosting) — no file, set these in the dashboard
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# On Mastra Cloud you set APP_SECRET + model access in the dashboard
# (Project → Settings → Env), not in a file — and the Mastra Gateway is auto-seeded,
# so a template can deploy and work with ZERO model keys. For storage you either bring
# your own Turso (set the two vars above in the dashboard) OR attach a CLI-managed
# database, which Mastra provisions and injects for you. Deploy from your machine with:
#   mastra auth            # once — stores a LOCAL cli token, not an app env var
#   mastra deploy --org <id> --project <name>
# (mastra auth's MASTRA_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN is a laptop CLI credential for pushing a
#  deploy — it is NOT something the running app reads.)

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — has a default; set only to override (local + prod alike)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Chat model as a `provider/model` string (Mastra model router — 600+ models). Forms:
#   GATEWAY (1 key, any provider):
#     CHAT_MODEL=vercel/openai/gpt-4.1-mini    → uses AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY     (Vercel AI Gateway)
#     CHAT_MODEL=mastra/openai/gpt-4.1-mini    → uses MASTRA_GATEWAY_API_KEY (Mastra Gateway)
#   DIRECT (one key per provider):
#     CHAT_MODEL=openai/gpt-4.1-mini           → uses OPENAI_API_KEY
#     CHAT_MODEL=groq/llama-3.3-70b            → uses GROQ_API_KEY
#     CHAT_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash       → uses GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY
# Full list: https://mastra.ai/models/environment-variables
# NOTE: image generation always uses OpenAI (needs OPENAI_API_KEY); native web search
# is OpenAI/Anthropic-only. The core chat works with any provider.
# CHAT_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=

# Harness workspace — the sandbox the agent reads/writes files + runs commands in.
# WORKSPACE_ROOT=./agent-workspace          # gitignored; relative resolves to absolute
# BROWSER_CLI=agent-browser                 # CLI the agent shells out to
# BROWSER_HEADLESS=true                     # false pops a real Chrome window
# BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH=                  # if Playwright can't find a Chrome

# Dolt — optional versioned business database (mysql2 → dolt sql-server). All unset =
# Dolt off (its tools error clearly if called). In the compose stack HOST/PORT/USER
# are set for you; you just add:
# DOLT_PASSWORD=
# DOLT_DATABASE=appdb

# Auth — set a ≥32-char secret to gate every /api/* route + Studio behind a Bearer JWT.
# Unset = open local dev. Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
# MASTRA_JWT_SECRET=

# Misc
# LOG_LEVEL=info                            # debug | info | warn | error
# MASTRA_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1               # for locked-down networks (blocks PostHog)

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Testing (you don't set these — the test runner does)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# `pnpm test` flips USE_AIMOCK on and points the SDKs at the local mock server itself,
# so real API calls never fire. Only uncomment to run the DEV server against the mock
# manually:
# USE_AIMOCK=true
# AIMOCK_URL=http://localhost:4010
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4010/v1
